                "e5d96d743a3d500fea4fe6e6314812f2742c1e78"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/01/86401/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "createdOn": 1767712425,
            "author": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks like a lot if not all of these are fan control related, so it is strange that the config owners never noticed this while doing fan testing.\n\nI believe the nice thing to do is to find owners for these files and have them provide a new name or maybe OK the current drop of the entry."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> Looks like a lot if not all of these are fan control related, so it is strange that the config owners never noticed this while doing fan testing.\n\nYeah, I'm guessing it's not actually problematic that they are duplicate names.  If I look at the `fbtp.json` as an example, there are two blobs with the same name, but they are different types: one is the Fan, the other is the PID Config for that Fan.  Not sure why this is necessarily \"bad\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> there are two blobs with the same name, but they are different types\n\nThanks for bringing this up, i did not consider it initially. My mistake \ud83d\ude1e.\n\n> Looks like a lot if not all of these are fan control related, so it is \nstrange that the config owners never noticed this while doing fan \ntesting.\n\nLooks like same name + different type is not a bug currently.\n\nAdjusted the script to provide an error when same name + same type is \nused and simply print a warning when the same name is used with a \ndifferent type.\n\nLong term i want to get rid of the cases where same name + different type is used.\n\nI don't think we need this flexibility and it complicates the EM implementation since an EM config record cannot be assumed to own the object path where its DBus interfaces are stored.\n\nPlease mark this comment as resolved in case you agree, otherwise let's discuss why we would need this capability for 2 config records to share the same object path \ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> simply print a warning when the same name is used with a\ndifferent type.\n\nI don't think that this point we even want it to be a warning.  Warning would imply that we think it's incorrect, and I don't think that's the case here.  EM has provisions for handling collisions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Just because it works does not mean it's a good idea. IMO we should look for the simplest possible solution which is to avoid exposes records sharing object paths.\n\nIf we need this capability to share an object path then yeah we can think about it but currently i don't see the need for it.\n\nUnfortunately some configs are currently not following that pattern and sharing object paths between different records. The warnings are intended to allow folks some time to migrate that and re-name these config records."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_medusa_board.json",
                    "line": 994,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marshall Zhan",
                        "email": "marshall.zhan.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "MarshallZhan-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Yosemite5 has fixed the typo for the DIMM. \nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/86088\nPlease keep this piece of code; it should be able to pass the tests."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_medusa_board.json",
                    "line": 994,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks, in latest revision, yv5 file is no longer changed."
                }
            ],
